    "body": "Fix pushed on branch `cut/0.23-heavy-lanes`, commit `7c46c4d4c` (base `origin/release/v0.23.0`). There is no PR: the cut takes the commit.\n\nCause: PR #2013 (#2004). The ladder starts one stepdown under Top Z. The air level at Top Z is gone. #2013 updated the debug twins (`level_links::the_helix_entry_is_one_continuous_descent`, `a_window_too_narrow_for_the_helix_is_refused_by_name_before_planning`) but not these two ignored tests. No toolpath behaviour is lost.\n\nChanges:\n\n- `adaptive_hsm.rs` `a_small_helix_rectangle_never_crosses_itself`: `helices == 3` changes to `helices == 2`. A new assert pins that the two helices land on Z -2 and Z -4.\n- `rotary_adaptive.rs` `the_r62_neck_levels_are_hsm_planned_on_microlift_returns`: \"the skin level stays HSM-planned\" (a level at radius 6.2 with arcs) changes to \"no level on the r6.2 skin (#2004)\" (no level at radius 6.2 with moves). The asserts on the 5.7 and 5.2 levels do not change. The ignore reason says \"two HSM plans\" now; the lane does not change.\n\nThe `#[test]` count does not change. No `#[ignore]` is removed.\n\nReadings (release, Windows, `-j 6`):\n\n- `a_small_helix_rectangle_never_crosses_itself --ignored --exact`: ok (1.65 s).\n- `the_r62_neck_levels_are_hsm_planned_on_microlift_returns --ignored --exact`: ok (25.9 s). Levels 5.700 and 5.200 are HSM-planned, load 17.3 % and 17.7 % D, 0 breaks.\n- `adaptive_hsm` whole binary: `--ignored` 5 passed; default 2 passed, 5 ignored.\n- `rotary_adaptive` whole binary: `--ignored` 3 passed; default 3 passed, 3 ignored.\n\nNot run: the app heavy lanes. The preflight gate had not reached them when this was written.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
