    "updated_at": "2026-11-17T18:28:34Z",
    "body": "Finding for the red step `pocket3d_hsm` (release, `--ignored`, run 44127297984):\n\n- Test: `the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean`.\n- Linux result: `(4726, 4698, 549)`. The pin was `(16029, 15372, 1427)`.\n\nCause: #2004 (PR #2013). The depth ladder now starts one stepdown under Top Z when no stock stands over Top Z. In this job, Top Z and the stock top are both Z 20. Thus the old level at Z 20 cut only air, and PR #2013 removed it. The expectation was stale. The toolpath is correct.\n\nProof on Windows x86_64, release. Columns are moves / planar feeds / arcs.\n\n| Level | `f887908f9` (parent of the #2013 merge) | `7c46c4d4c` |\n|---|---|---|\n| Z 20 (with microlifts at Z 20.3 to 21.2) | 11303 / 10672 / 878 | gone |\n| Z 15 | 383 / 376 / 74 | 383 / 376 / 74 |\n| Z 10 | 3567 / 3560 / 327 | 3567 / 3560 / 327 |\n| Z 5 | 383 / 376 / 74 | 383 / 376 / 74 |\n| Z 0 | 377 / 376 / 74 | 377 / 376 / 74 |\n| Total | 16017 / 15360 / 1427 | 4716 / 4688 / 549 |\n\n- The Z 20 level fed at Z 20 over the top face of the part (X -25 to 25, Y -25 to 14.7). All its moves are at Z 20 or higher. The stock top is Z 20, so this level removed no material.\n- From the first feed at Z 15 to the end, the 4710 moves are identical at the two commits. A hash of their Debug form is the same.\n- Only the entry before Z 15 changed: 4 moves before, 6 moves now.\n- Every level verifies clean. No level falls back to rings. The planner budget is not reached.\n\nFix: commit `207596999` on `cut/0.23-heavy-lanes`.\n\n- Windows pin: `(4716, 4688, 549)`. Two runs gave the same result.\n- Linux pin: `(4726, 4698, 549)`, from the cut runner.\n- The macOS aarch64 pin is stale, and we cannot measure it here. macOS now uses the band arm: each measured triple, plus or minus 10. Issue #2371 asks for the macOS measurement.\n- No other test pins a move count for one platform.\n",
